{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20355",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.96,
      "end_seconds": 5.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.38,
      "end_seconds": 10.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.02,
      "end_seconds": 21.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Mainly burning pain in the upper tummy. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.47,
      "end_seconds": 29.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.53,
      "end_seconds": 33.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "I'm on naproxen, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.54,
      "end_seconds": 36.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.58,
      "end_seconds": 46.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "It's 250 milligrams. Pantoprazole. I take it it 40 milligrams, before breakfast for my acidity."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.25,
      "end_seconds": 50.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.12,
      "end_seconds": 57.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "I'd say about four days. Actually, no, closer to to two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.22,
      "end_seconds": 72.46,
      "duration_seconds": 13.24,
      "text": "alright, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse these questions might sound routine, but they matter"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.94,
      "end_seconds": 90.69,
      "duration_seconds": 16.75,
      "text": "yes, spicy food and empty stomach. That makes it worse. I get some relief from milk. And I've been feeling full quickly as well, for two weeks. About feeling full quickly, it's severe, honestly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.03,
      "end_seconds": 94.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Did you notice any weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.36,
      "end_seconds": 100.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "No weight loss, thankfully."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.93,
      "end_seconds": 104.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "any difficulty swallowing, vomiting blood or jaundice?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.08,
      "end_seconds": 111.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.41,
      "text": "I haven't had difficulty swallowing, vomiting blood or jaundice, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.07,
      "end_seconds": 118.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "I follow. Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.9,
      "end_seconds": 120.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.32,
      "end_seconds": 126.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.35,
      "end_seconds": 143.03,
      "duration_seconds": 12.68,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.82,
      "end_seconds": 148.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.67,
      "end_seconds": 157.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "I have arthritis in my knees sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit i've got acid reflux"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.03,
      "end_seconds": 165.88,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "right, right. Yes, arthritis in your knees is known to us, good to have that clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.05,
      "end_seconds": 181.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Okay, are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.71,
      "end_seconds": 184.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "No allergies at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.16,
      "end_seconds": 206.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Okay, has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.27,
      "end_seconds": 210.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.15,
      "end_seconds": 214.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.5,
      "end_seconds": 220.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "yes, I had a bunion operation, six years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.16,
      "end_seconds": 227.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.09,
      "end_seconds": 230.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.88,
      "end_seconds": 250.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with some tenderness in the upper middle part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.39,
      "end_seconds": 255.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "okay, you can sit up now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.78,
      "end_seconds": 275.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "Okay, thinking it through, my working impression is dyspepsia possibly related to anti-inflammatory tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.33,
      "end_seconds": 278.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.5,
      "end_seconds": 291.64,
      "duration_seconds": 12.14,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's dyspepsia possibly related to anti-inflammatory tablets, and we'll know more once the a test for the stomach germ is back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.39,
      "end_seconds": 322.39,
      "duration_seconds": 15.0,
      "text": "let's get a test for the stomach germ, for dyspepsia. Please stop taking the anti-inflammatory tablets for now and use paracetamol for the pain. Let's review you in four weeks. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.11,
      "end_seconds": 328.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Uh, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}